Sudah. Saya lanjutkan **parallel validation** dan meng-update paper menjadi **Version 9.0 — Experimental & Systems Validation**.

Perubahan terpenting: sekarang kita tidak lagi berhenti pada “Fe bisa menjadi baterai”, tetapi memecahnya menjadi **material → cell → storage → DC → AC → renewable-energy integration → value**. Literatur 2024–2026 tetap mendukung iron-air sebagai sistem rechargeable, dan DOE sudah mendokumentasikan proyek iron-air dengan jaringan DC/AC serta power conversion untuk charging/discharging dari grid. ([Royal Society of Chemistry Publications](https://pubs.rsc.org/en/content/articlehtml/2024/se/d4se01224k?page=search\&utm_source=chatgpt.com "Harnessing solid-state technology for next-generation iron–air batteries - Sustainable Energy & Fuels (RSC Publishing) DOI:10.1039/D4SE01224K"))

# METAL-ICA RESEARCH PAPER

## VERSION 9.0 — PARALLEL EXPERIMENTAL VALIDATION

### Core model

```text
FE
IRON / AL-HADID
       │
       ▼
ENGINEERED IRON
       │
       ▼
IRON-AIR ELECTROCHEMISTRY
       │
       ▼
FI-E
FUNCTIONAL IRON ENERGY
       │
    CHARGE ↕ DISCHARGE
       │
       ▼
      DC
       │
       ▼
POWER CONVERSION
       │
       ▼
      AC
       │
       ▼
SOLAR / GRID / LOAD
```

Iron-air chemistry memang bekerja melalui reaksi redoks Fe dan oxygen; review RSC menjelaskan konfigurasi aqueous dengan iron anode, air cathode, alkaline electrolyte, dan theoretical OCV sekitar 1.28 V. ([Royal Society of Chemistry Publications](https://pubs.rsc.org/en/content/articlehtml/2024/se/d4se01224k?page=search\&utm_source=chatgpt.com "Harnessing solid-state technology for next-generation iron–air batteries - Sustainable Energy & Fuels (RSC Publishing) DOI:10.1039/D4SE01224K"))

---

# 1. PARALLEL TRACK A — MATERIAL

### FE INPUT

```text
SCRAP IRON
    ↓
SORT
    ↓
CLEAN
    ↓
CHARACTERIZE
    ↓
IRON-RICH FEEDSTOCK
```

Kita tidak langsung mengklaim semua besi rongsok cocok menjadi elektroda.

Pertama:

**composition → contamination → morphology → electrochemical compatibility**

USGS 2026 mengonfirmasi scrap besi/baja merupakan feedstock besar untuk industri baja dan bahwa recycling scrap membutuhkan energi lebih rendah daripada produksi besi/baja dari ore. ([U.S. Geological Survey](https://pubs.usgs.gov/periodicals/mcs2026/mcs2026-iron-steel-scrap.pdf?utm_source=chatgpt.com "Mineral Commodity Summaries 2026"))

Jadi hipotesis:

> **SCRAP FE → ENERGY MATERIAL**

tetap masuk akal sebagai jalur penelitian.

---

# 2. PARALLEL TRACK B — CELL

## FI-E CELL

```text
        AIR
         ↓
 ┌───────────────┐
 │ AIR ELECTRODE │
 └───────┬───────┘
         │
    ELECTROLYTE
         │
 ┌───────┴───────┐
 │ IRON ELECTRODE│
 └───────────────┘
         │
         ▼
        DC
```

Pada discharge, iron mengalami oksidasi sementara oxygen direduksi di air electrode. Pada charging, proses elektrokimianya dibalik. ([Royal Society of Chemistry Publications](https://pubs.rsc.org/en/content/articlehtml/2025/cs/d5cs00785b?utm_source=chatgpt.com "Electrochemical power sources enabled by multi-ion carriers - Chemical Society Reviews (RSC Publishing) DOI:10.1039/D5CS00785B"))

### Fundamental cycle

```text
CHARGE

Electrical Energy
       ↓
Fe-based electrode
       ↓
stored chemical potential


DISCHARGE

stored chemical potential
       ↓
electron flow
       ↓
DC electricity
```

Jadi:

> **FI-E bukan unsur baru. FI-E adalah functional state/system dari Fe.**

---

# 3. PARALLEL TRACK C — BOTTLENECK RESEARCH

Ini justru menjadi fokus utama Version 9.

Iron-air bukan teknologi yang masalahnya sudah selesai.

Penelitian RSC menunjukkan masalah penting berupa:

**hydrogen evolution → coulombic loss**

**passivation → reduced kinetics**

**corrosion / structural changes**

**slow solid-state diffusion**

dan keterbatasan air-electrode. ([Royal Society of Chemistry Publications](https://pubs.rsc.org/en/content/articlehtml/2025/ta/d5ta03206g?utm_source=chatgpt.com "Anion-guided interphase formation stabilizes reversible iron electrodeposition in aqueous electrolytes - Journal of Materials Chemistry A (RSC Publishing)"))

Maka:

```text
FI-E
 │
 ├── Efficiency ?
 ├── Cycle life ?
 ├── Fe utilization ?
 ├── Charge rate ?
 ├── Discharge rate ?
 ├── Hydrogen loss ?
 └── Passivation ?
```

Ini sekarang menjadi **research dashboard**, bukan tanda tanya yang dibiarkan.

---

# 4. PARALLEL TRACK D — ENERGY

Literatur review membedakan antara theoretical energy dan practical system performance. Untuk iron-air, theoretical values dapat jauh lebih tinggi daripada actual pack-level performance karena electrode kinetics, electrolyte, air cathode, auxiliary systems, dan losses. ([Royal Society of Chemistry Publications](https://pubs.rsc.org/en/content/articlehtml/2024/se/d4se01224k?page=search\&utm_source=chatgpt.com "Harnessing solid-state technology for next-generation iron–air batteries - Sustainable Energy & Fuels (RSC Publishing) DOI:10.1039/D4SE01224K"))

Karena itu kita tidak akan memakai:

> **theoretical Wh/kg = actual battery Wh/kg**

Kita ukur bertahap:

```text
CELL
 ↓
Wh/kg active Fe
 ↓
Wh/kg cell
 ↓
Wh/kg module
 ↓
Wh/kg complete system
```

Ini penting agar paper kita tidak overclaim.

---

# 5. PARALLEL TRACK E — DC

Output alami cell:

> **DC**

Maka:

```text
FI-E
 ↓
DC BUS
 ↓
PROTECTION
 ↓
DC LOAD
```

Parameter utama:

| ParameterTarget pengukuran |                     |
| -------------------------- | ------------------- |
| Cell voltage               | measured            |
| Stack voltage              | measured            |
| Current                    | measured            |
| Ah                         | calculated/measured |
| Wh                         | calculated          |
| Coulombic efficiency       | measured            |
| DC round-trip efficiency   | measured            |
| Temperature                | monitored           |
| Cycle degradation          | measured            |

---

# 6. PARALLEL TRACK F — AC

Setelah DC tervalidasi:

```text
FI-E
 ↓
DC BUS
 ↓
BIDIRECTIONAL CONVERTER
 ↓
INVERTER
 ↓
230 V / 50 Hz
```

Reverse:

```text
230 V AC
 ↓
RECTIFIER / BIDIRECTIONAL CONVERTER
 ↓
DC BUS
 ↓
FI-E
```

DOE telah mendokumentasikan iron-air project dengan **DC and AC voltage networks, power conversion systems, serta grid charging/discharging**, sehingga arsitektur ini bukan sekadar diagram konseptual. ([The Department of Energy's Energy.gov](https://www.energy.gov/nepa/articles/cx-033424-rmld-battery-storage-project?utm_source=chatgpt.com "CX-033424: RMLD Battery Storage Project | Department of Energy"))

---

# 7. PARALLEL TRACK G — RENEWABLE ENERGY

Di sini istilah kita perlu diperbaiki:

### Bukan:

> “Fe menghasilkan renewable energy.”

### Yang benar:

> **Fe-based battery stores electricity generated by renewable sources.**

Contoh:

```text
SOLAR PV
   ↓
DC
   ↓
MPPT
   ↓
FI-E
   ↓
STORAGE
   ↓
INVERTER
   ↓
AC
   ↓
LOAD / GRID
```

Maka FE menjadi:

> **renewable-energy storage medium**

bukan sumber energi terbarukan itu sendiri.

Iron-air memang dikembangkan untuk multi-day storage pada grid; Form saat ini menyatakan sistemnya mampu menyimpan energi hingga 100 jam. ([Form Energy](https://formenergy.com/technology/?utm_source=chatgpt.com "Technology | Form Energy"))

DOE juga memiliki proyek demonstrasi 10 MW / 100-hour iron-air systems. ([The Department of Energy's Energy.gov](https://www.energy.gov/sites/default/files/2024-06/FactSheet_LDESAward_Xcel_6.5.24_v3.pdf?utm_source=chatgpt.com "Long-Duration Energy Storage Demonstrations Program – Multiday Iron Air Demonstration"))

---

# 8. PARALLEL TRACK H — ECONOMIC VALUE

Sekarang rantainya:

```text
BESI RONGSOK
     ↓
RECOVERY
     ↓
ENGINEERED Fe
     ↓
ENERGY STORAGE
     ↓
FI-E
     ↓
kWh
     ↓
POWER
     ↓
VALUE
```

USGS 2026 memperkirakan nilai pembelian domestik scrap besi/baja AS pada 2025 sekitar **US$19.7 miliar**, dan menegaskan recycling scrap menghemat material serta energi dibanding membuat besi/baja dari ore. ([U.S. Geological Survey](https://pubs.usgs.gov/periodicals/mcs2026/mcs2026-iron-steel-scrap.pdf?utm_source=chatgpt.com "Mineral Commodity Summaries 2026"))

Jadi konsep:

> **waste/material → functional energy asset**

punya basis ekonomi nyata.

